<urn:sha256:49a072d08e26ec357944f2cc6d46a0b17d9daf61b4a29a676b5a69949c44bfa4> <urn:ledger:ns#statement> "accepted-by is a claimed identity resolved by email from git config and trusted on review, corroborated mechanically by refusing model and CI identities and by requiring an acceptance's actor to match the author of the commit that introduced it; the signature field is reserved and empty so a cryptographic upgrade is additive rather than a migration." .
