<urn:sha256:cc9afc0da9e021e8bab76f2c23962f60e89e3711a1f3150ab1e451838152a58f> <urn:ledger:ns#hash> "sha256:cc9afc0da9e021e8bab76f2c23962f60e89e3711a1f3150ab1e451838152a58f" .
<urn:sha256:cc9afc0da9e021e8bab76f2c23962f60e89e3711a1f3150ab1e451838152a58f> <urn:ledger:ns#ofDecision> <urn:dec:hafeok.ledger/01KZPMKQGDY97FFRJYE2RQ5W0Q> .
<urn:sha256:cc9afc0da9e021e8bab76f2c23962f60e89e3711a1f3150ab1e451838152a58f> <urn:ledger:ns#set> <urn:ledger-set:ledger-design> .
<urn:sha256:cc9afc0da9e021e8bab76f2c23962f60e89e3711a1f3150ab1e451838152a58f> <urn:ledger:ns#statement> "Cross-entry referential integrity is a distinct graph stage of verify — G001 dangling supersession target, G002 dangling parent hash, G003 undeclared decision identity — closed at three, reported by the same command with unchanged exit semantics, and deliberately outside the file gate's ten-class import surface so an outside implementation of the format need not run a graph." .
<urn:sha256:db533d1bf931164969445d87819fada9ecceaec88d77c267d01f70a74dfcb6fa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
